            <ArticleTitle>Randomized controlled trial assessing a traditional Chinese medicine remedy in the treatment of primary dysmenorrhea.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>762-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A proof-of-concept study to assess the safety and efficacy of a traditional Chinese medicine formula as treatment for primary dysmenorrhea showed no statistically significant benefit over placebo. However, some efficacy parameters suggested possible superiority of the active treatment and so a larger study needs to be performed to determine whether this remedy has a role in the treatment of dysmenorrhea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
